        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-76523-2">
            <title>[6] Giant negative photomagnetism in an alterlattice</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-76523-2</link>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><b>Last authors:</b> Liping Li, Guangshe Li</p><p><b>Authors:</b> Junhong Zhou, Xu Han, Haibin Huang, et al.</p><p><span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'>Score 6/10</span> <b>C_MAYBE</b></p><p><b>Why:</b> Altermagnetism is relevant; experimental study of magnetic response in complex oxides.</p><p><b>Tags:</b> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#altermagnetism</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#magnetism</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#oxide</span></p><p><img src='https://pubads.g.doubleclick.net/gampad/ad?iu=/285/nature_communications/article&amp;sz=728x90&amp;c=-2014304312&amp;t=pos%3Dtop%26type%3Darticle%26artid%3Ds41467-026-76523-2%26doi%3D10.1038/s41467-026-76523-2%26techmeta%3D128,135,137,140,144,145,146,147,28%26subjmeta%3D1101,119,263,301,357,400,537,624,638,639,766,915,94,997%26kwrd%3DChemical+physics,Magnetic+properties+and+materials,Magneto-optics,Solid-state+chemistry,Structural+properties' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /></p><hr/><p><b>Abstract:</b> The authors identify an alterlattice in lanthanum–calcium titanate and report a reversible photoinduced decrease in magnetic susceptibility, with evidence for enhanced short-range antiferromagnetic correlations.</p>]]></content:encoded>
